{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused SDPA path changes attention rounding enough that downstream projections amplify it beyond the final tolerance, so I’m not spending a verification attempt on it. A safer optimization is to make each head’s Q/K/V matrices contiguous before the same `matmul → scale → softmax → matmul` sequence; this keeps the arithmetic order while giving rocBLAS dense head-major matrices. I’m checking bitwise behavior and timing locally first."}}
