{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"agent_message","text":"CUDA Graph replay is exact, but on medium and long cases its output-copy cost cancels the launch savings, so I won’t spend a verification attempt on that form. I’m checking one more exact arithmetic-preserving route: combine projection GEMMs and split their outputs. This can reduce GEMM launches, but I’ll keep it only if rocBLAS returns bitwise-identical columns and the required weight/output rearrangement is genuinely faster."}}
